      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change is intended to handle the case where a slot with a single presence GPIO can accept drives from different vendors, and some of those drives do not provide a FRU. In that situation, the installed drive cannot be identified from a FRU that is present.\n\nHowever, I wonder whether this fits EM\u0027s general approach of probing based on information it actually detects from the device. With NOT, the drive type is inferred from the absence of something rather than from a positively identified characteristic.\n\nIt also relies on the probe author knowing exactly which drive variants can occupy that slot.\n\nAs mentioned in the other comments, some corner cases may also be difficult to handle robustly, such as a misplaced NOT condition or an object that appears after the initial scan.\n\nOne alternative might be for the platform to expose the installed drive type explicitly, for example through a virtual sensor, and then have the EM probe match that information positively. Since this would be configured per platform rather than in common code, other platforms would not be affected, although a virtual sensor is a semantically less precise way to express the drive type.\n\nI\u0027d be interested in hearing how the maintainers view this kind of use case.",
      "revId": "ea835262e9a023cbdeb9b8373a3a1f0cc375245f",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
