      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T10:12:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m concerned about whether this case can actually happen. If the probed D-Bus object appears after EM\u0027s first scan, a config published because the object was absent would be pruned on the next rescan, which could emit an `InventoryAdded` followed by an `InventoryRemoved` event for something that should never have existed. If it can really happen, it seems we would need a way to resolve it, otherwise these events would be unexpected.",
      "revId": "ea835262e9a023cbdeb9b8373a3a1f0cc375245f",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce5d18b4_beef7db2",
        "filename": "src/entity_manager/perform_probe.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002134
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T10:12:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A NOT that is not followed by TRUE, FALSE or a D-Bus probe is ignored, so NOT FOUND(\u0027x\u0027) behaves as FOUND(\u0027x\u0027) with no log message.\n\nI feel silently ignoring it is not great, but I\u0027m not sure which behavior the maintainers prefer. Would rejecting it when the probe is parsed be better, or is ignoring acceptable?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ea835262e9a023cbdeb9b8373a3a1f0cc375245f",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
