      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T14:20:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the probe statement does not parse or pass checks, IMO best to drop that config at the earliest chance we get and log an error.\n\nWe could modify the logic around\n```\n  Configuration::Configuration(\n      const std::vector\u003cstd::filesystem::path\u003e\u0026 configurationDirectories,\n      const std::filesystem::path\u0026 schemaDirectory) :\n      schemaDirectory(schemaDirectory),\n      configurationDirectories(configurationDirectories)\n  {\n      loadConfigurations();\n      filterProbeInterfaces();\n  }\n```\n\nto ensure configurations with probes that have errors do not get emplaced into `configurations` data structure in the first place and then we do not have to deal with it later.\n\nCurrently `filterProbeInterfaces` simply skips over probes that do not parse, and the config remains part of `configurations`.",
      "parentUuid": "ce5d18b4_beef7db2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 27
